{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(arr, n, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an element x is the majority element in a sorted array arr of length n.\n    The majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _first_occurrence(array, length, target):\n        \"\"\"\n        Finds the index of the first occurrence of target in a sorted array.\n        Returns -1 if the target is not found.\n        \"\"\"\n        low, high = 0, length - 1\n        result = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = (low + high) // 2\n            if array[mid] == target:\n                result = mid\n                high = mid - 1  # Search in the left half for the first occurrence\n            elif array[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:\n                high = mid - 1\n        return result\n\n    first_idx = _first_occurrence(arr, n, x)\n\n    # If x is not present in the array, it cannot be a majority element\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    # Check if the element at first_idx + n//2 is also x\n    # This implies that x occurs at least (n//2) + 1 times\n    # (from first_idx to first_idx + n//2 inclusive)\n    if (first_idx + (n // 2) < n) and (arr[first_idx + (n // 2)] == x):\n        return True\n    else:\n        return False"}
