{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets all even (1-based) bits within the input number's effective bit width.\"\"\"\n    # Determine the effective bit width, ensuring a minimum of 1 for n=0.\n    # bit_length() returns 0 for n=0, so max(1, ...) handles this case.\n    effective_bit_width = max(1, n.bit_length())\n\n    # Generate a mask with bits set at 0-based indices 1, 3, 5, ...\n    # These correspond to 1-based even positions 2, 4, 6, ...\n    mask = 0\n    # Loop from 0-based index 1 up to (but not including) effective_bit_width,\n    # incrementing by 2 to hit only the odd indices.\n    for i in range(1, effective_bit_width, 2):\n        mask |= (1 << i)\n\n    # Apply the generated mask to the number using a bitwise OR operation.\n    return n | mask"}
