{"task_id": "Mbpp/264", "solution": "import math\ndef dog_age(human_years: float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates a dog's age in dog years based on a specific algorithm.\n    The first two human years count as 21 dog years, and each subsequent human year as 4 dog years.\n    \"\"\"\n    FIRST_TWO_YEARS_DOG_YEARS = 21.0\n    ADDITIONAL_PER_YEAR = 4.0\n    YEARS_PRORATED_THRESHOLD = 2\n\n    # Compute raw dog years based on the algorithm\n    if human_years <= 0:\n        raw_dog_years = 0.0\n    elif human_years <= YEARS_PRORATED_THRESHOLD:\n        # Prorate the first two human years\n        raw_dog_years = (human_years / YEARS_PRORATED_THRESHOLD) * FIRST_TWO_YEARS_DOG_YEARS\n    else:\n        # Add 21 for the first two years, then 4 for each subsequent year\n        raw_dog_years = FIRST_TWO_YEARS_DOG_YEARS + (human_years - YEARS_PRORATED_THRESHOLD) * ADDITIONAL_PER_YEAR\n    \n    # Round to the nearest integer, with halves rounding up.\n    return int(math.floor(raw_dog_years + 0.5))"}
