{"task_id": "Mbpp/395", "solution": "from typing import Optional\ndef first_non_repeating_character(s: str, ignore_case: bool = False) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first non-repeated character in a given string.\n    The search can be case-sensitive or case-insensitive.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return None\n\n    # Use a dictionary to store character counts.\n    # Python dicts (from 3.7+) preserve insertion order, which is essential for finding the \"first\" character.\n    counts = {}\n\n    if ignore_case:\n        # First pass: populate counts for casefolded characters.\n        for char_original in s:\n            char_folded = char_original.casefold()\n            counts[char_folded] = counts.get(char_folded, 0) + 1\n\n        # Second pass: find the first character from the original string\n        # whose casefolded version has a count of 1.\n        for char_original in s:\n            char_folded = char_original.casefold()\n            if counts[char_folded] == 1:\n                return char_original\n    else:\n        # First pass: populate counts for case-sensitive characters.\n        for char in s:\n            counts[char] = counts.get(char, 0) + 1\n\n        # Second pass: find the first character with a count of 1.\n        for char in s:\n            if counts[char] == 1:\n                return char\n\n    # If no non-repeating character is found, return None.\n    return None"}
