{"task_id": "Mbpp/462", "solution": "def combinations_list(items_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates all possible combinations (subsets) of elements from the input list,\n    preserving a specific ordering as demonstrated in the design context example.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(items_list)\n    all_combinations = []\n\n    # Iterate through all possible masks from 0 to 2^n - 1.\n    for mask in range(1 << n):\n        current_subset = []\n        # For each mask, build the subset by checking bits from the highest index down to 0.\n        for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n            if (mask >> i) & 1:  # If the i-th bit is set in the mask\n                current_subset.append(items_list[i])\n        all_combinations.append(current_subset)\n    return all_combinations"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/460", "solution": "from typing import Any, List\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(message)\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return self.message\ndef Extract(data: List[List[Any]], skip_empty: bool = False) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts the first element from each sublist in a list of lists.\n    Raises InvalidInputError for invalid input structures or empty sublists if skip_empty is False.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(data, list):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Top-level input must be a list of lists.\")\n\n    result: List[Any] = []\n    for i, sublist in enumerate(data):\n        if not isinstance(sublist, list):\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Item at index {i} is not a list.\")\n\n        if not sublist:\n            if skip_empty:\n                continue\n            else:\n                raise InvalidInputError(f\"Sublist at index {i} is empty\")\n        result.append(sublist[0])\n    return result"}
