{"task_id": "Mbpp/807", "solution": "from typing import List, Optional\ndef first_odd(numbers: List[int]) -> Optional[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first odd integer in a list of numbers.\n    Returns the first odd integer found, or None if no odd number is present.\n    \"\"\"\n    for number in numbers:\n        # Check if the integer value of the number is odd.\n        # This implicitly converts items to int, raising errors for non-convertible types.\n        if int(number) % 2 != 0:\n            return int(number)\n    return None"}
